          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "पधारणो (padhārṇo) is inherited from a reconstructed paddhārayati, \"steps\"; CDIAL lists the Old Marwari verb padhāraï, \"comes, goes\" (CDIAL 7768). It is the polite word for a guest's coming."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
